==Enemy==
Assassin Bear has incredible speed and DPS. At 100% strength magnification, he deals a meager 3,000 area damage per hit, which might not seem like much, yet he keeps himself very safe at 800 range, almost ''double'' that of [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] (500), and his attack rate allows for over 10,000 damage per second, shredding many units with ease.

This enemy is usually used as a means of guaranteeing defeat, by spawning en masse and/or at extremely high buffs once a time limit or condition is reached, sometimes pre-announced by a [[Ms. Sign]], making him a makeshift time limit. However, this does not happen in every stage. There are also stages in which he is actually meant to be defeated, such as [[Twilight Poachers]], [[Littering Coast]], [[False Resurrection]], and [[Sea Cave Habitat]].

In stages like [[Merciless Onslaught]], [[Ashen Rain]], [[Veggie Friends]] and [[Forever Fishing]], he is used as a gimmick, in which either a massive horde of Assassin Bears or an extremely buffed one spawns as soon as an enemy perishes, due to the enemy limit, leading into an instant defeat. This means you need to use the enemy limit to your advantage and keep the enemies alive.

==Strategy==
The default [[Cat Cannon]]'s [[Wave Attack]] can kill most Assassin Bears easily, however at higher strength magnifications Assassin Bear can survive it, meaning a certain defeat if he does spawn. Thankfully, overbuffed Assassin Bears are always easy to avoid fighting in the first place, except in [[Surrealist Sins]] if you're not careful. Another way to beat him is to use a [[Cat Units|Cat Unit]] that can reach and kill the Assassin Bear without dying; options include cats with very few knockbacks and either fast speed or high health (at least against [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark Enemies]]). The higher the speed, the lower the health needed. [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Glass Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Express Cat]], [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Sanada Yukimura]], [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Jamiera Cat]] are some examples.

Using [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attack Cats]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attack Cats]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion Cats]] works too, as long as he isn't too buffed. If the Assassin Bear comes out when the base receives enough damage and the Wave/Surge/Explosion spawns, he will likely step into the attack and die instantly, as his immense speed and high damage will cause him to easily clip through units. In other scenarios, it's still possible to hit the bear by using other enemies to generate the wave/surge just as the he appears. Outranging him is another option. It is rare, but there are some cats that can do it. One common option is [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], provided if you're able to somehow stall him.

The last option is using a unit to clip through the Assassin Bear after being knocked back so they get a chance to hit him. The best choice for this would be [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]], as while other options can still work, they must have high speed and a short foreswing so they can catch Assassin Bear as soon as they recover from a knockback.

