==Trivia==
*His Japanese name, Burakkuma (ブラックマ), is derived from ブラック ''burakku'' (black), 熊 ''kuma'' (bear) and possibly リラックマ ''Rirakkuma'' ([[wikipedia:Rilakkuma|Rilakkuma]], a [[wikipedia:San-X|San-X]] character).
*He may be a reference to [[wikia:dragonball:Mercenary Tao|Mercenary Tao]] from ''[[wikia:dragonball|Dragon Ball]]''. Assassin Bear has red eyes and is otherwise entirely black except for his mouth, much like Mercenary Tao's appearance after becoming a cyborg. Furthermore, Assassin Bear's Japanese description says that he charges 100 million per kill, the same amount charged by Mercenary Tao in the Japanese version of ''Dragon Ball''.
*His design bears resemblances to the Japanese mascot [[wikipedia:Kumamon|Kumamon]] and may be a reference to it.
*The line "Licensed to kill" may be a reference to the [[wikipedia:James Bond|James Bond]] franchise, where the titular James Bond also owns a licence to kill.
*In the [https://youtube.com/watch?v=JBBwbMHnnws?t=1m58s launch trailer], an Assassin Bear and 2 Shy Boys clear the entire battlefield of Cats before [[The Cat God (Special Cat)|The Cat God]] comes onto the scene.
*He was technically the only [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemy to appear in [[Ganso!! Nyanko Daisensou]] and [[Kumanchu Royale]], where the Dark trait didn't exist yet. His design would then be used as the basis for most Dark enemies after [[Version 2.0 Update|Version 2.0]].
**[[Higher Score|Challenge Battle]] can be considered the first stage in the game to contain a Dark enemy, even though Assassin Bear was originally [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]].
*At 150 speed, Assassin Bear is the fastest character in the entire game.
*He has the lowest possible money drop in the game, along with many other enemies.
**However, prior to his money drop nerf, he drops enough money to refill one's wallet on death.
*In [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou]], Assassin Bear's role as a timed menace was filled by a rainbow Type 2 [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Penanggalan|Penanggalan]] that had much shorter range but pushed just as hard, if not harder.
*One of the possible [[Cat Shrine#Cat Fortune|Cat Fortunes]] is "You're Assassin Bear's next target..."

